  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When using the OnVariableChange call back for variables, synced variable changes and SetProgramVariable() both will update the variable and call the callback. These methods will also update the old value saved, but only before calling the callback and not after. The old value is left in a bad state. This means that a combination of SetProgramVariable/OnDeserialization followed with changing the value directly in Graph (or CyanTriggers) will not have the proper old value during the change callback.\nNote, this affects both UdonGraph and CyanTriggers.\nVRChat build 1114\nVRCSDK3 2021.07.13.13.39\nSee screenshot for example graph. The graph contains an interact to change the variable directly, a \"Toggle\" event to change the variable using SetProgramVariable, and an OnVariableChange event to react to either. If you call the \"Toggle\" event and then call the \"Interact\" event, the OnVariableChange event will have both value and oldValue equal to the same data.",
